1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Hex Machina is an agent evaluation environment disguised as a spell game.
The executable graph is shared by a person and their agent.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:18,000
This spell should water a rare Moonflower.
Instead, twelve lunar ducks flood the observatory.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Moth suggests suspicious runes. WebMCP tools inspect the exact graph
and trace the responsible path. The simulator remains authoritative.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:42,000
The human contributes taste: “The ducks are funny.”
They become sacred, so deleting them is no longer valid.

5
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:57,000
The agent ranks bounded rewrites. The eight-edit umbrella route
is the only eligible candidate and waits for approval.

6
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:08,000
The application proves sacred reachability and applies atomically.
The recast is Stable: the room is dry and all twelve ducks remain.

7
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Three causal rules and ninety-six variants separate grounded agents
from unsafe shortcuts. Hex Machina is a deterministic gym.
